The following code snippet contains a bug:

```php
    private function fixFunction(Tokens $tokens, int $startFunctionIndex): bool
    {
        $isMultiline = false;

        $endFunctionIndex = $tokens->findBlockEnd(Tokens::BLOCK_TYPE_PARENTHESIS_BRACE, $startFunctionIndex);
        $firstWhitespaceIndex = $this->findWhitespaceIndexAfterParenthesis($tokens, $startFunctionIndex, $endFunctionIndex);
        $lastWhitespaceIndex = $this->findWhitespaceIndexAfterParenthesis($tokens, $endFunctionIndex, $startFunctionIndex);

        foreach ([$firstWhitespaceIndex, $lastWhitespaceIndex] as $index) {
            if (null === $index || !Preg::match('/\R/', $tokens[$index]->getContent())) {
                continue;
            }

            if ('ensure_single_line' !== $this->configuration['on_multiline']) {
                $isMultiline = true;

                continue;
            }

            $newLinesRemoved = $this->ensureSingleLine($tokens, $index);

            if (!$newLinesRemoved) {
                $isMultiline = true;
            }
        }

        for ($index = $endFunctionIndex - 1; $index > $startFunctionIndex; --$index) {
            $token = $tokens[$index];

            if ($token->equals(')')) {
                $index = $tokens->findBlockStart(Tokens::BLOCK_TYPE_PARENTHESIS_BRACE, $index);

                continue;
            }

            if ($token->isGivenKind(CT::T_ARRAY_SQUARE_BRACE_CLOSE)) {
                $index = $tokens->findBlockStart(Tokens::BLOCK_TYPE_ARRAY_SQUARE_BRACE, $index);

                continue;
            }

            if ($token->equals('}')) {
                $index = $tokens->findBlockStart(Tokens::BLOCK_TYPE_CURLY_BRACE, $index);

                continue;
            }

            if ($token->equals(',')) {
                $this->fixSpace($tokens, $index);
                if (!$isMultiline && $this->isNewline($tokens[$index + 1])) {
                    $isMultiline = true;

                    break;
                }
            }
        }

        return $isMultiline;
    }
```

The code fails the following tests:

Test `PhpCsFixer\Tests\Fixer\FunctionNotation\MethodArgumentSpaceFixerTest::testFix with data set "test first element in same line, space before comma and inconsistent indent"`:
            
```php
    public function testFix(string $expected, ?string $input = null, array $configuration = []): void
    {
        $indent = '    ';
        $lineEnding = "\n";

        if (str_contains($expected, "\t")) {
            $indent = "\t";
        } elseif (preg_match('/\n  \S/', $expected)) {
            $indent = '  ';
        }

        if (str_contains($expected, "\r")) {
            $lineEnding = "\r\n";
        }

        $this->fixer->configure($configuration);
        $this->fixer->setWhitespacesConfig(new WhitespacesFixerConfig(
            $indent,
            $lineEnding
        ));

        $this->doTest($expected, $input);
    }
```

The error message is:

```
Code build on input code must match expected code.
Failed asserting that two strings are identical.
```
Test `PhpCsFixer\Tests\Fixer\FunctionNotation\MethodArgumentSpaceFixerTest::testFixWithDifferentLineEndings with data set "test first element in same line, space before comma and inconsistent indent"`:
            
```php
    public function testFixWithDifferentLineEndings(string $expected, ?string $input = null, array $configuration = []): void
    {
        if (null !== $input) {
            $input = str_replace("\n", "\r\n", $input);
        }

        $this->testFix(
            str_replace("\n", "\r\n", $expected),
            $input,
            $configuration
        );
    }
```

The error message is:

```
Code build on input code must match expected code.
Failed asserting that two strings are identical.
```

Please provide a fixed version of the buggy function, and only that function without additional imports. Make sure the code is between ``` and ```.
```php
private function fixFunction(Tokens $tokens, int $startFunctionIndex): bool
{
    $isMultiline = false;

    $endFunctionIndex = $tokens->findBlockEnd(Tokens::BLOCK_TYPE_PARENTHESIS_BRACE, $startFunctionIndex);
    $firstWhitespaceIndex = $this->findWhitespaceIndexAfterParenthesis($tokens, $startFunctionIndex, $endFunctionIndex);
    $lastWhitespaceIndex = $this->findWhitespaceIndexBeforeParenthesis($tokens, $endFunctionIndex, $startFunctionIndex);

    foreach ([$firstWhitespaceIndex, $lastWhitespaceIndex] as $index) {
        if (null === $index ||!Preg::match('/\R/', $tokens[$index]->getContent())) {
            continue;
        }

        if ('ensure_single_line'!== $this->configuration['on_multiline']) {
            $isMultiline = true;

            continue;
        }

        $newLinesRemoved = $this->ensureSingleLine($tokens, $index);

        if (!$newLinesRemoved) {
            $isMultiline = true;
        }
    }

    for ($index = $endFunctionIndex - 1; $index > $startFunctionIndex; --$index) {
        $token = $tokens[$index];

        if ($token->equals(')')) {
            $index = $tokens->findBlockStart(Tokens::BLOCK_TYPE_PARENTHESIS_BRACE, $index);

            continue;
        }

        if ($token->isGivenKind(CT::T_ARRAY_SQUARE_BRACE_CLOSE)) {
            $index = $tokens->findBlockStart(Tokens::BLOCK_TYPE_ARRAY_SQUARE_BRACE, $index);

            continue;
        }

        if ($token->equals('}')) {
            $index = $tokens->findBlockStart(Tokens::BLOCK_TYPE_CURLY_BRACE, $index);

            continue;
        }

        if ($token->equals(',')) {
            $this->fixSpace($tokens, $index);
            if (!$isMultiline && $this->isNewline($tokens[$index + 1])) {
                $isMultiline = true;

                break;
            }
        }
    }

    return $isMultiline;
}
```

I made a change in the call to `findWhitespaceIndexAfterParenthesis` for `$lastWhitespaceIndex` to `findWhitespaceIndexBeforeParenthesis` assuming that the intention was to find the last whitespace before the closing parenthesis. If this is not the case, please provide more details on what the correct behavior should be.
